---
const traits = ["Creative", "Product-minded", "Thoughtful", "Data-driven", "AI-native"];

const caseStudies = [
  {
    no: "01",
    title: "Data Requests",
    tag: "AI tool design",
    summary: "Model context is its UI.",
    blocks: [
      { h: "The system" },
      { p: "Our application lets students make submissions to update their data. Keeping student data up to date is essentially the main function of the app, and what advisers spend significant amounts of time doing — so this was an opportunity to take some work off their plate. These student submissions get stored as diffs on their own model and get merged to their target once an adviser approves (or rejects) the request." },
      { p: "It's a simple framework that has a fair bit of complexity in its implementation: open and rejected requests need distinct form states, requests to create records appear to students as actual records but with a pending-approval label, many different endpoints for different data types, etc." },
      { visual: "diff" },
      { h: "The attempt" },
      { p: "Our initial AI tool design explained the system, gave context to the student and adviser submission workflow, and handed over all of the student's data — existing records, diffs on those, the status of the submissions, when to use the id of the submission in the tool vs. the id of the record, etc. The thesis was: we're using a smart model, give it all the info and let it run." },
      { p: "Actual use showed consistent confusion on the model's part. It struggled to make sense of all we had dumped on it and to explain it succinctly to students. It would mix up the status of a submission with the status of a college application; it would share model data and just state “some updates are pending.”" },
      { h: "The lesson" },
      { p: "Model context is its UI. Our student UI shows only what they need to see — if they've made a request to change data, we don't need to show the old data; requests to add new records look as much like actual records as possible. We were piling on complexity that our UI had already handled for it by the back end." },
      { p: "Solution: update the agent surface to mirror the UI. Don't explain inner workings that should not be surfaced to the student. Handle the complexity in code in the name of a simple surface, and let the agent focus on its prime directive — not on decoding complex rules." },
    ],
  },
  {
    no: "02",
    title: "Smart Interaction",
    tag: "Feature craft",
    summary: "A vague brief — “make interaction-logging better.” [draft — not yet Fraser's voice]",
    blocks: [
      { p: "Brief was vague — advisers log an “interaction” every time they talk to a student, and the ask was just “can we make this better with AI?” No spec, no interface in mind." },
      { p: "Usage data showed the actual friction: some advisers were doing this in batches — open the form, log one interaction, close it, reopen, log the next. Rather than guess at one fix, built for three different habits at once: extended the existing bulk-import tool to fully support interaction records via a table view; added a “keep window open” toggle for advisers who prefer the one-at-a-time dialog but want less friction; and, for single entries, added AI smart-fill from notes." },
      { visual: "notes" },
      { p: "The real Linear ticket that kicked this off exists as a screenshot (colleague's handle needs redacting before use) — worth showing as proof alongside the narrative rather than just describing it." },
    ],
  },
  {
    no: "03",
    title: "Tasks system",
    tag: "Greenfield",
    summary: "A new student portal needed “tasks” — nobody could define what that meant. [draft — not yet Fraser's voice]",
    blocks: [
      { p: "A new student portal needed a “tasks” concept to guide students through their journey. Neither the client nor the designer could really define what a task should be: the client couldn't articulate it, and the designer didn't have enough visibility into the actual advising workflow to fill the gap. Fell to me to define it." },
      { visual: "tasks" },
      { p: "Reasoning: the app's whole job is collecting and tracking student data. A checklist that doesn't feed that data isn't actually helping anyone. So tasks shouldn't be an arbitrary to-do list — they should be a read of the student's actual data. A task is pending or complete based on whether the underlying data condition is met, and completing a task just means updating the relevant data." },
      { p: "Built v1 hardcoded — a fixed set of tasks mapped to fixed data conditions — but shaped so it could grow into something configurable later, by exposing the filtering tools we'd already built as a task-config screen down the line." },
    ],
  },
  {
    no: "04",
    title: "Scripts to prompts",
    tag: "Strategic reframe",
    summary: "Push AI Chatbot over SMS.",
    blocks: [
      { h: "The problem" },
      { p: "Client uses a legacy student messaging platform to send script-based SMS messages to students to guide them in their college journey. My investigation showed that this had an abysmally low engagement rate. We'd just built out a student-facing AI chatbot, and already had an SMS messaging system in Grace. Let's connect the dots — replace the outdated, underperforming system with something better, which doesn't require manually exporting students from our system into another, which can communicate intelligently, reference students' actual data, and make use of the full toolset we've built for the chatbot, feeding data back into our system and contributing to measurable outcomes the client cared about." },
      { h: "How" },
      { p: "This was an open question. Client rep works with the scripts every day and required guidance into the world of AI prompts." },
      { h: "Solution" },
      { p: "Two new modes in our Campaign scheduler: “from AI” — sends messages to students based on highly configurable targeting filters. That message may be pre-composed or AI generated per student based on a prompt — the agent has access to retrieval tools and can reference actual student data. E.g. “this message is targeting students who have 'in-progress' college applications. Let's move those toward 'applied.' Look up the student's college applications and offer to help them finish, referencing the schools they have applications in progress for, as character limits allow.”" },
      { visual: "sms" },
      { p: "The old system couldn't come close to this. The agent always has its system prompt attached and understands its directive of helping students and keeping their data up to date. Where we have talking points we wish the agent to hit in this specific conversation, we attach an additional “per-conversation” prompt that persists across future messages — “script”-like control with a fraction of the work involved." },
      { p: "The second AI sending mode I pitched and built out — the client chose to call it “automated touch points.” It shares the same filters and prompts field but functions on an ongoing basis and unlocks functionality the previous system couldn't come close to touching. Rather than sending at a specific date and time, these campaign messages go out whenever a student newly matches the filter condition." },
      { p: "There's considerably more here — e.g. how we solved for wrong numbers. We don't want to expose student info to the wrong person by mistake. Solution: just ask for their name and validate that against our records. A wrong number isn't going to guess that right. Simple, easy “two-factor.”" },
    ],
  },
];

const heritage = [
  {
    img: "/images/translash.jpeg",
    title: "TransLash",
    year: "2024",
    detail: "Lead developer on a bold new site designed by Alix Hopfengaertner-Vigneault and Kaila Jacques. 2025 Webby Award. Legislation-tracking dashboard pulling daily from an external API into interactive D3 charts.",
    link: "https://translash.org/",
  },
  {
    img: "/images/acumen.jpg",
    title: "Acumen",
    year: "2023",
    detail: "Custom WordPress REST API and a multi-component Vue.js map app for global programs and portfolio companies.",
    link: "https://acumen.org/where-we-work/",
  },
  {
    img: "/images/artsmidwest.jpeg",
    title: "Arts Midwest",
    year: "2023",
    detail: "Award-winning site; custom REST API powering an interactive SVG grantee-impact map.",
    link: "https://artsmidwest.org/impact/",
  },
];

const personal = [
  {
    img: "/images/wedding.png",
    title: "Wedding RSVP",
    detail: "A playful RSVP site for my own wedding — save-as-you-go forms, custom guest links, a heart you can shoot an arrow through to make us kiss.",
    link: "https://kasia-fraser.love/rsvp/v4jXBVDBjTyz7YDY9vDxVjmm",
  },
  {
    img: "/images/spf.jpeg",
    title: "Chart labels that don't overlap",
    detail: "When Chart.js couldn't place doughnut-chart labels without overlap, I wrote the placement geometry myself.",
    link: "https://helpstpauls.com/annual-report/#by-the-numbers",
  },
];
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>Fraser Page</title>
		<style is:global>
			@font-face {
				font-family: "Recursive";
				font-style: normal;
				font-weight: 300 1000;
				font-display: swap;
				src: url("/fonts/recursive-latin.woff2") format("woff2");
			}

			:root {
				--bg: #ffffff;
				--fg: #111111;
				--muted: #5a5a5a;
				--line: #111111;
				--win-shadow: 4px 4px 11px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
			}

			:root[data-theme="dark"] {
				--bg: #111111;
				--fg: #f0f0f0;
				--muted: #a3a3a3;
				--line: #f0f0f0;
				--win-shadow: 4px 4px 14px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);
			}

			@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
				:root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
					--bg: #111111;
					--fg: #f0f0f0;
					--muted: #a3a3a3;
					--line: #f0f0f0;
					--win-shadow: 4px 4px 14px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);
				}
			}

			* {
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			html,
			body {
				margin: 0;
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--fg);
			}

			body {
				font-family: "Recursive", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 380, "MONO" 0, "CASL" 0;
				font-size: 16px;
				line-height: 1.55;
				padding: 2.5rem 2rem 6rem;
			}

			a {
				color: inherit;
				text-decoration: underline;
				text-underline-offset: 2px;
			}

			.topbar {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: space-between;
				align-items: baseline;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
				margin-bottom: 4.5rem;
				font-size: 0.8rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.02em;
			}

			.topbar-name {
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 700;
			}

			.theme-links button {
				font: inherit;
				background: none;
				border: none;
				color: inherit;
				cursor: pointer;
				padding: 0;
				text-decoration: underline;
				text-underline-offset: 2px;
			}

			.theme-links .sep {
				margin: 0 0.35rem;
				color: var(--muted);
			}

			.theme-links button[aria-current="true"] {
				text-decoration: none;
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 700;
			}

			.hero {
				max-width: 46rem;
				margin-bottom: 6rem;
			}

			.hero-line {
				font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
				line-height: 1.15;
				margin: 0 0 2rem;
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 500;
				display: flex;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 0.5rem;
			}

			.hero-line select {
				font: inherit;
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 500;
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--fg);
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
				appearance: auto;
				max-width: 100%;
			}

			.tagline {
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
			}

			.subline {
				color: var(--muted);
				max-width: 34rem;
				margin: 0;
			}

			h2.section-label {
				font-size: 0.8rem;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				letter-spacing: 0.06em;
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 700, "MONO" 1;
				margin: 0 0 2rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				padding-top: 1rem;
			}

			section {
				margin-bottom: 5.5rem;
			}

			.latest p {
				max-width: 42rem;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.case-list {
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
			}

			.case-row {
				font: inherit;
				color: inherit;
				background: none;
				border: none;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				text-align: left;
				width: 100%;
				padding: 1.5rem 0;
				cursor: zoom-in;
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr auto;
				gap: 0.75rem;
				align-items: baseline;
			}

			.case-list .case-row:last-child {
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
			}

			.case-row:hover .case-title {
				text-decoration: underline;
				text-underline-offset: 3px;
			}

			.case-row:focus-visible {
				outline: 1px dashed var(--line);
				outline-offset: 4px;
			}

			.case-no {
				font-variation-settings: "MONO" 1;
				color: var(--muted);
			}

			.case-title {
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 600;
			}

			.case-tag {
				font-variation-settings: "MONO" 1;
				font-size: 0.8rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				white-space: nowrap;
			}

			.case-summary {
				grid-column: 2 / 4;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 0.9rem;
				margin-top: 0.4rem;
			}

			table.listing {
				width: 100%;
				border-collapse: collapse;
				font-size: 0.9rem;
			}

			table.listing th {
				text-align: left;
				font-size: 0.75rem;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				letter-spacing: 0.05em;
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 700, "MONO" 1;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				padding: 0 0.75rem 0.75rem 0;
			}

			table.listing td {
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				padding: 1.25rem 0.75rem 1.25rem 0;
				vertical-align: top;
			}

			table.listing img {
				width: 3.5rem;
				height: 3.5rem;
				object-fit: cover;
				display: block;
			}

			table.listing td.detail {
				color: var(--muted);
				max-width: 30rem;
			}

			table.listing td.year {
				font-variation-settings: "MONO" 1;
				color: var(--muted);
				white-space: nowrap;
			}

			.close p {
				max-width: 36rem;
			}

			footer {
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				padding-top: 1rem;
				margin-top: 4rem;
				font-size: 0.8rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				display: flex;
				justify-content: space-between;
			}

			/* Case study windows */
			.win {
				position: fixed;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--fg);
				box-shadow: var(--win-shadow);
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				overflow: hidden;
				min-width: 20rem;
				min-height: 12rem;
			}

			.win-titlebar {
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 0.75rem;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
				cursor: move;
				user-select: none;
				font-variation-settings: "MONO" 1, "wght" 700;
				font-size: 0.75rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.03em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				flex: 0 0 auto;
			}

			.win-controls {
				display: flex;
				gap: 0.4rem;
				flex: 0 0 auto;
			}

			.win-controls button {
				font: inherit;
				background: var(--bg);
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				color: inherit;
				width: 0.75rem;
				height: 0.75rem;
				border-radius: 50%;
				line-height: 1;
				cursor: pointer;
				padding: 0;
			}

			.win-controls button:hover {
				background: var(--fg);
			}

			.win-title {
				overflow: hidden;
				text-overflow: ellipsis;
				white-space: nowrap;
			}

			.win-body {
				padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
				overflow: auto;
				flex: 1;
			}

			.win-tag {
				font-variation-settings: "MONO" 1;
				font-size: 0.8rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				display: block;
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
			}

			.win-body h4 {
				font-size: 0.75rem;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				letter-spacing: 0.05em;
				font-variation-settings: "wght" 700, "MONO" 1;
				color: var(--muted);
				margin: 1.75rem 0 0.6rem;
			}

			.win-body h4:first-of-type {
				margin-top: 0;
			}

			.win-body p {
				margin: 0 0 1rem;
				max-width: 36rem;
			}

			.win-visual {
				margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem;
				max-width: 30rem;
			}

			.win-visual svg {
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				display: block;
			}

			.resize-handle {
				position: absolute;
			}

			.rh-n { top: -3px; left: 6px; right: 6px; height: 6px; cursor: ns-resize; }
			.rh-s { bottom: -3px; left: 6px; right: 6px; height: 6px; cursor: ns-resize; }
			.rh-e { top: 6px; bottom: 6px; right: -3px; width: 6px; cursor: ew-resize; }
			.rh-w { top: 6px; bottom: 6px; left: -3px; width: 6px; cursor: ew-resize; }
			.rh-ne { top: -3px; right: -3px; width: 10px; height: 10px; cursor: nesw-resize; }
			.rh-nw { top: -3px; left: -3px; width: 10px; height: 10px; cursor: nwse-resize; }
			.rh-se { bottom: -3px; right: -3px; width: 10px; height: 10px; cursor: nwse-resize; }
			.rh-sw { bottom: -3px; left: -3px; width: 10px; height: 10px; cursor: nesw-resize; }

			@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
				* {
					transition: none !important;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="topbar">
			<span class="topbar-name">Fraser Page</span>
			<span class="theme-links" id="theme-links">
				<button type="button" data-theme-choice="light" aria-current="false">Light</button>
				<span class="sep">/</span>
				<button type="button" data-theme-choice="dark" aria-current="false">Dark</button>
			</span>
		</div>

		<div class="hero">
			<p class="hero-line">
				<select id="trait-select" aria-label="Choose a trait">
					{traits.map((t, i) => (
						<option value={t} selected={i === 0}>{t}</option>
					))}
				</select>
				<span>developer</span>
			</p>
			<p class="tagline">Throw me your fuzziest briefs. (What? No, not underpants.)</p>
			<p class="subline">I start with the data, not assumptions, then build the elegant version, front to back.</p>
		</div>

		<section class="latest">
			<h2 class="section-label">Latest</h2>
			<p>Most recently, I led development on Grace, an AI-native platform advisers use to support hundreds of thousands of students nationally through the college application process &mdash; hundreds of advisers use it day to day. Built for a client with no in-house product team, working alongside Springloaded's design team on everything from a greenfield student portal to an AI assistant to the adviser tools below.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="case-studies">
			<h2 class="section-label">Case studies</h2>
			<div class="case-list">
				{caseStudies.map((c, i) => (
					<button type="button" class="case-row" data-case-index={i}>
						<span class="case-no">{c.no}</span>
						<span class="case-title">{c.title}</span>
						<span class="case-tag">{c.tag}</span>
						<span class="case-summary">{c.summary}</span>
					</button>
				))}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="heritage">
			<h2 class="section-label">Heritage</h2>
			<table class="listing">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th></th>
						<th>Project</th>
						<th>Detail</th>
						<th>Year</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{heritage.map((h) => (
						<tr>
							<td><img src={h.img} alt={h.title} /></td>
							<td><a href={h.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{h.title}</a></td>
							<td class="detail">{h.detail}</td>
							<td class="year">{h.year}</td>
						</tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</section>

		<section class="personal">
			<h2 class="section-label">Craft &amp; experiments</h2>
			<table class="listing">
				<tbody>
					{personal.map((p) => (
						<tr>
							<td><img src={p.img} alt={p.title} /></td>
							<td><a href={p.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{p.title}</a></td>
							<td class="detail">{p.detail}</td>
						</tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</section>

		<section class="close">
			<h2 class="section-label">Get in touch</h2>
			<p>I'm looking for a team that cares as much about the decision as the delivery &mdash; where design carries real weight, and there's room to grow past &ldquo;developer.&rdquo; If that sounds like your team: <a href="mailto:fp@fraser.page">fp@fraser.page</a></p>
		</section>

		<footer>
			<span>Toronto, Canada (Remote)</span>
			<span>Built by Fraser Page</span>
		</footer>

		<template id="visual-sms">
			<svg viewBox="0 0 480 200" role="img" aria-label="Comparison of a rigid script message versus an AI prompt message">
				<text x="70" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Recursive" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1" fill="var(--muted)">SCRIPT</text>
				<rect x="10" y="32" width="200" height="158" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"></rect>
				<rect x="24" y="54" width="172" height="66" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"></rect>
				<text font-family="Recursive" font-size="10" fill="var(--fg)">
					<tspan x="34" y="73">Reminder: complete</tspan>
					<tspan x="34" y="87">your application by</tspan>
					<tspan x="34" y="101">the deadline.</tspan>
				</text>
				<text x="34" y="140" font-family="Recursive" font-size="9" fill="var(--muted)">Same message,</text>
				<text x="34" y="152" font-family="Recursive" font-size="9" fill="var(--muted)">every student.</text>

				<text x="410" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Recursive" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1" fill="var(--muted)">PROMPT</text>
				<rect x="270" y="32" width="200" height="158" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"></rect>
				<rect x="284" y="54" width="172" height="82" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"></rect>
				<text font-family="Recursive" font-size="10" fill="var(--fg)">
					<tspan x="294" y="71">Hi Maria — you're close</tspan>
					<tspan x="294" y="85">to finishing your Ohio</tspan>
					<tspan x="294" y="99">State application. Want</tspan>
					<tspan x="294" y="113">help with the last part?</tspan>
				</text>
				<text x="294" y="152" font-family="Recursive" font-size="9" fill="var(--muted)">Written per student,</text>
				<text x="294" y="164" font-family="Recursive" font-size="9" fill="var(--muted)">from their actual data.</text>
			</svg>
		</template>

